The encoded data is in the form of an AC-3 audio file
which can be played back with mpv or other players.

To decode:
ffmpeg and fldigi can be used for decoding the generated file.

0. Install dependencies
  * apt-get install ffmpeg fldigi # for Ubuntu

1. Convert to .WAV:
  * ffmpeg -f ac3 -i challenge.bin challenge.wav

2. Open fldigi:
  * fldigi

3. Skip the "Setup Wizard" if presented
  * Press "Finish"

4. Select mode of operation
  * In the menu, press "Op Mode" -> "RTTY" -> "RTTY-45"
  * Under the frequency indicator (default 14070.000)
    there is a dropdown menu where the default is "USB".
    Select "LSB".

5. Load the audio
  * In the menu, press "File" -> "Audio" -> "Playback"
  * Select out.wav
  * Prompt: "Play continuous loop?", press "Yes"

6. Align the decoder
  * In the black-blue-yellow waterfall at the bottom of the
    fldigi-window, align the vertical bars to the center of
    the yellow stripes and single-click.

7. Done
  You should now see the message being decoded in the fldigi UI.

